The counter starts at 0 and is clamped between 0 and the given cap, inclusive. An inc operation increases the counter by one, unless it is already at capacity, and a dec operation decreases the counter by one, unless it is already at zero. Resetting sets the value back to zero from whatever it is.

The loop above processes each event in turn. Inc and dec both adjust the value only when bounded by 0 and cap, so they never go out of range. Resetting is checked last so it is never shadowed, and the 'else' branch does nothing. The final value, within range by construction, is then returned.

